  "implemented": [
    "Migration7 adds one append-only generation seal table; versions1–6/checksums/table tuples remain frozen.",
    "Explicit trusted terminal lifecycle capability retains the admitted original binding, rejects copying/serialization and foreign PID before locks; deterministic realm/generation UUID supports same-generation bootstrap retry.",
    "Generation membership gate serializes seal with new raw/mapped reservations, fresh coverage and first activation. Existing receipt/active acknowledgements, reads and original closure remain allowed.",
    "New credits and active memberships cannot revive a sealed generation; exact existing credit ACK and revocation remain available; another generation is unaffected.",
    "Runtime role has SELECT+INSERT on facts only; UPDATE/DELETE/dangerous privileges and PUBLIC/column ACL drift are rejected, including NULL/empty ACL handling. Protected historical authority tables stay readonly.",
    "Bridge quiesces transport and the mapped coordinator, refuses new operator requests, joins the accepted control call and rereads late coverage before the final paid query. Full participant/owner/monitor close and joins happen in finally.",
    "Unexpected controller loss skips an unfunded seal; absent coordinator/global close uncertainty creates no seal SQL. Ordinary API.stop remains reusable and never seals.",
    "The first supervision error survives a secondary seal/shutdown failure with a fixed note forbidding metadata retirement."
  ],
  "evidence_boundaries": [
    "Final distinct cases only; all628previous case identities retained, no FAIL/ERROR/SKIP. Prior attempts remain history and are not summed.",
    "Actual existing PostgreSQL with real advisory lock wait observation, two transaction contenders and read-only observer; this is protocol concurrency, not physical multi-node acceptance.",
    "Actual funded control connection has control_connection_loans=1 during seal SQL; credits/usage remain unchanged, then ordinary lifecycle drains.",
    "Actual local prepare retains the same control lane across preparing and active commits; seal queues behind it, records while an admitted body remains live, denies a later body before SQL, and permits original release with metadata1 still charged.",
    "Postcommit binding acknowledgement loss is reproduced after the real transaction commits; a fresh bootstrap acknowledges the original stable seal once. This is not a claimed network-driver commit-loss experiment.",
    "Controller/reader/cancellation/secondary-failure tests use real lifecycle objects with controlled channel transport and probes; no new provider or native sandbox acceptance.",
    "Opaque authority is a trusted-server Python boundary, not a PostgreSQL cryptographic predicate or RLS. The cooperating runtime SQL role can insert a negative fact directly."
  ],
  "remaining": [
    "The seal is not physical closure: control/read/completion SQL can still run while its original funding remains held. A future exact whole-generation physical witness and independently funded audited credit custodian are required.",
    "No coordinator, lost control, unresolved storage close or unconfirmed seal leaves credits charged; process PID/TTL/runtime.retired is never sufficient.",
    "No historical RECONCILE_REQUIRED jobs were closed/replayed. Unknown native cleanup, quotas, elastic placement, physical M1/M2/M3, SDK/UI and global acceptance remain open."
  ],
